cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this app, please cite it and the works it builds on, listed under references.
type: software
title: stim-events
abstract: Finds the stimulation epochs of physiological recordings and their parameters (amplitude and unit,
  pulse width, pulse rate, train duration, duty cycle on/off, number of pulses, polarity, waveform, site,
  contact, condition) and writes them as one BIDS-style events.tsv, for nerve stimulation and
  neuromodulation experiments in any species. Reads trigger/TTL lines, stimulus monitors and parameter
  envelope channels of NWB files (as written by physio-import), per-trial parameters stored with the
  recording, user parameter tables (CSV/XLSX) described by a stim-map.yaml, imported markers, file and
  folder names, and, optionally, SPARC Data Structure metadata; merges them by priority and reports
  overlapping trains, trains without a clean baseline and table vs channel disagreements. One step of
  the Cardiovascular Response to Nerve Stimulation workflow. Research outputs.
